# <type>(<scope>): <subject>   (≤72 chars, imperative, no trailing period)
#
# --- Body (optional): what changed and why. Wrap at ~72 columns. ---
#
#
# --- Footers (optional) ---
# BREAKING CHANGE: <describe the incompatible change>
# Refs: #<issue>
# Closes: #<issue>
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Conventional Commits — allowed types:
#   feat     A new user-facing feature
#   fix      A bug fix
#   docs     Documentation only
#   style    Formatting/whitespace; no behavior change
#   refactor Neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
#   perf     A performance improvement
#   test     Add or correct tests
#   build    Build system, esbuild, bundling, dependencies
#   ci       CI configuration and scripts
#   chore    Maintenance not touching src/ behavior
#   revert   Reverts a previous commit
#
# Suggested scopes (warning only — a new scope is allowed when none fits):
#   editor, sidebar, webview          product surfaces
#   services, models, protocol        shared layers
#   specs, build, deps, docs, test    project & tooling
#   agentic                           instructions, skills, agents, hooks
#
# Breaking change: add "!" after type/scope AND a BREAKING CHANGE footer.
#   e.g. feat(protocol)!: rename dependency payload
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
